---
// How to share a motion, in three steps: on /you/ itself for someone with no motions, in a dialog for someone with some.
import Agents from './Agents.astro';
import {skillInstall, skillShare} from '../lib/catalogue.mjs';
interface Props { title: string; titleId: string; skip?: boolean }
const {title, titleId, skip = false} = Astro.props;
---
<div class="share-guide">
  <div class="share-intro">
    <h2 id={titleId}>{title}</h2>
    <p>A motion is the look of a film you made: its colours, type and movement, never its story. Your agent writes it from your project, and nothing is published until you say yes and the pull request is merged.</p>
    <p class="share-need">You need an agent that can run commands, a cloud one included. No git, GitHub CLI or token: you sign in with GitHub here to open the pull request.</p>
    <a href="/docs/contribute/">Read the full guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <span class="label">Install the motionhub skill, once per computer{skip && <small>Skip this if you have it already</small>}</span>
      <div class="code"><pre data-copy tabindex="0"><code>{skillInstall}</code></pre></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="label share-ask">Open the project of your film, and ask your agent<Agents /></span>
      <div class="code"><pre data-copy tabindex="0"><code>{skillShare}</code></pre></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="label">Check the result, then say yes</span>
      <p>Your agent runs the checks and shows you the result. With your yes, it gives you a link and a code: open the link, sign in with GitHub, type the code, and the pull request opens under your name. Follow it under Shared; it joins Your motions once merged.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</div>
